\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Policy stamp}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{provenance}

\p{A \strong{policy stamp} #{\nu} is a content-addressed description of an
executable policy: model artifact, tokenizer, action serializer, decoding
settings, and implementation revision. Resolving the stamp produces the
action law #{\pi^\nu(\,\cdot\mid\mathsf H_t)} for every public history in its
declared domain.}

\p{Two stamps are equal only when every component that may change the action
law is equal. A display name or checkpoint step is therefore insufficient.}
